You need a pool where EVERY submitted task either gets a worker immediately or is rejected outright - no waiting in a queue under any circumstance. Which queue type fits, and why?

Real code:

ThreadPoolExecutor executor = new ThreadPoolExecutor(
        2, 5, 60, TimeUnit.SECONDS,
        new LinkedBlockingQueue<Runnable>(3));    // capacity 3 = bounded, same class as experiment 8

for (int i = 1; i <= 9; i++) {
    try {
        executor.execute(new SleepTask(i));       // each sleeps 5 seconds
        PoolState.print("accepted task " + i, executor);
    } catch (RejectedExecutionException e) {
        Log.line("!!! Task " + i + " REJECTED");
    }
}

private static void runWorkload(String label, BlockingQueue<Runnable> queue) {
    ThreadPoolExecutor executor = new ThreadPoolExecutor(
            2, 5, 60, TimeUnit.SECONDS, queue);
    int accepted = 0, rejected = 0;
    for (int i = 1; i <= 9; i++) {
        try {
            executor.execute(new SleepTask(i));
            accepted++;
        } catch (RejectedExecutionException e) {
            rejected++;
        }
    }
    Log.line(label + " accepted=" + accepted + "  rejected=" + rejected);
}

// called once with new ArrayBlockingQueue<Runnable>(3)
// called once with new LinkedBlockingQueue<Runnable>(3)

